= render 'shared/fun_stuff_page', page_title: 'Privacy Policy', current_page: 'Privacy Policy', page_subtitle: 'How Baldrick Buddy handles information on phone, tablet, or desktop', document_title: 'Privacy Policy — Baldrick Buddy', eye_label: 'Baldrick Buddy', parent_title: 'Baldrick Buddy', parent_path: fun_stuff_baldrick_buddy_path, meta: ['Effective 4 August 2026', 'Baldrick Buddy', 'No account required'], toc: baldrick_buddy_privacy_toc do
  p.lead This privacy policy explains how Baldrick Buddy (“the app”) handles information when you use it on phone, tablet, or desktop.

  .prose
    .callout.info
      span.ic
        svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
          circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"
          path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"
      div
        span.lbl Details
        p.bd
          | Product: Baldrick Buddy · Operator: Baldrick (
          = link_to 'www.baldrickboard.com', 'https://www.baldrickboard.com', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener'
          | ) · Contact: via
          = link_to ' www.baldrickboard.com', 'https://www.baldrickboard.com', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener'

    section#summary
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot At a glance
        | Summary

      ul
        li Baldrick Buddy does
          strong  not
          |  require an account.
        li Baldrick Buddy does
          strong  not
          |  sell personal data.
        li Discovery and firmware updates talk to devices on
          strong  your local network
          | .
        li Limited optional contact with baldrickboard.com may occur (for example, checking for a newer version of the app).
        li Some information may be stored
          strong  only on your device
          |  to make the app work better.

    section#what-the-app-does
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Product
        | What the app does

      p Baldrick Buddy helps you find Baldrick lighting controllers on your local network, view basic status, open each board’s web interface in your browser, and start firmware updates.

    section#information-we-process
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Data
        | Information we process

      h3#on-your-device On your device

      p Depending on platform and version, the app may store locally:

      ul
        li Recently discovered board identifiers such as IP addresses and hostnames (so boards can reappear faster)
        li App preferences and settings
        li Temporary caches needed for scanning or update progress

      p This data stays on your device unless you choose to share it somehow outside the app (for example by copying an IP address).

      h3#on-your-local-network On your local network

      p To find and manage boards, the app may:

      ul
        li Send and receive local-network discovery traffic (including broadcast/multicast/UDP and Bonjour/mDNS-style service discovery where available)
        li Make HTTP requests to devices on your LAN (for example
          code  /system_state
          |  and update endpoints)
        li Scan nearby addresses on your local subnet when needed to locate boards

      p Traffic used for discovery and board control is intended to stay on your LAN. The app validates responses so non-Baldrick devices are not listed as boards after checks fail.

      h3#with-baldrickboard-com With baldrickboard.com

      p The app may occasionally contact baldrickboard.com (or related Baldrick-operated URLs) for product purposes such as:

      ul
        li Checking whether a newer version of Baldrick Buddy is available
        li Opening Baldrick website links you choose (for example support or product pages)

      p Those requests are not used to upload your board list or LAN inventory as a cloud sync feature.

    section#what-we-do-not-do
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Limits
        | What we do not do

      p Baldrick Buddy does not:

      ul
        li Create user accounts or require sign-in
        li Sell your personal information
        li Use your board discovery data for advertising
        li Require access to your contacts, photos, microphone, or camera for core features

    section#permissions
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Access
        | Permissions

      p Depending on the platform, the operating system may ask for permission to:

      ul
        li Access the
          strong  local network
          |  (required to discover and talk to boards)
        li Use related networking capabilities (for example multicast/broadcast where the platform requires approval)

      p If you deny local-network access, discovery and updates will not work correctly.

    section#children
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Age
        | Children

      p Baldrick Buddy is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.

    section#data-retention
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Retention
        | Data retention

      p Locally stored board history and preferences remain on your device until you clear app data, uninstall the app, or use an in-app option to clear them (where provided).

    section#third-parties
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Stores
        | Third parties

      p Store platforms (Apple App Store, Google Play, Microsoft Store, and similar) may collect their own analytics, crash, or purchase information under their policies when you download or update the app. That processing is controlled by those platforms, not by Baldrick Buddy’s discovery features.

    section#international-users
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Where
        | International users

      p Baldrick Buddy is offered internationally. Local storage and network requests happen on the device and network you use. Any contact with baldrickboard.com is processed in connection with operating that website and related product services.

    section#your-choices
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Control
        | Your choices

      p You can:

      ul
        li Revoke local-network (or related) permissions in system settings
        li Clear app data or uninstall the app to remove locally stored preferences and known-board history
        li Avoid optional website/update checks by not using those features, where the app makes them optional

    section#changes
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Updates
        | Changes to this policy

      p We may update this privacy policy from time to time. The version published on baldrickboard.com is the authoritative version. Material changes will be reflected by updating the effective date above.

    section#contact
      h2
        span.hk
          span.bar
          span.annot Reach us
        | Contact

      p
        | Privacy questions about Baldrick Buddy: use the contact options on
        = link_to ' www.baldrickboard.com', 'https://www.baldrickboard.com', target: '_blank', rel: 'noopener'
        | .

